    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "You can now change or remove charge lines on a draft invoice, and the stored invoice total is recalculated on the server each time. The acceptance test passes under `bin/e2e`. That test only covers removing a line, so I also tried an edit and a bad removal by calling the API directly against the running app. Changing a line to 2.5 \u00d7 $40 stored the right total ($150.00), and removing a line that doesn't exist returned 404. I haven't clicked through the Edit/Save/Cancel buttons in the browser.\n\n**Server** (Spring Boot \u2014 the app is Spring, not OfficeFloor, even though the package is named `net.officefloor`):\n- **New endpoints:** `PUT /api/projects/{projectId}/invoices/{invoiceId}/line-items/{lineItemId}` changes a line, and `DELETE` on the same path removes it. Both return the updated invoice with its lines. A change uses the same checks as adding a line.\n- **Rules:** both work only on draft invoices, the same as adding a line. On a sent or paid invoice they return 409, and an unknown line returns 404.\n- **Total:** `Invoice` now recalculates its stored amount whenever a line is added, changed or removed. That stored amount is what the project's invoice list and the dashboard show. The changes are in `Invoice.java`, `InvoiceLineItem.java`, `InvoiceService.java` and `InvoiceController.java`.\n\n**Front end** (`invoice-detail.ts`, `invoice.service.ts`):\n- On a draft invoice, each line has **Edit** and **Remove** buttons (`lineitem-edit-{id}`, `lineitem-remove-{id}`).\n- Edit switches the row into inline inputs with **Save** and **Cancel** (`lineitem-save-{id}`, `lineitem-cancel-{id}`). Enter saves and Escape cancels.\n- After each action, keyboard focus moves to a sensible place, and errors appear in a `role=\"alert\"` message (`lineitem-edit-error`). No existing `data-testid` was renamed or removed.\n\n**Database:** I didn't add a migration because the existing tables already support this. Invoices can already be worth $0, so removing every line works.\n\nNeither change nor removal writes an audit record; the spec doesn't ask for one.",
